@native-migration
Feature: Bounded native migration contracts and owned completion
  Scenario: Migration grants stay independent of agent workflow access
    Then migration requests without their complete independent grant never reach SDK preparation
  Scenario: Migration models retain native ports and workflow persistence
    Then migration models preserve all four native contracts graph persistence and named JSON fields
  Scenario: Imported native values retain private bounded matching
    Then imported private values keep bounded ownership and distinguish metadata from content bytes
  Scenario: Migration inputs retain all four methods and ten item types
    Then migration contracts preserve sources attribution details and all native item kinds
  Scenario: Invalid migration inputs name their offending nested field
    Then migration contracts reject malformed fields bounds accessors and inconsistent results
  Scenario: Nonempty imports wait for their matching terminal result
    Then migration acknowledgements progress completion and empty imports retain native ordering
  Scenario: Migration lifecycle rejects foreign replayed and unbounded events
    Then migration correlation rejects unknown incomplete duplicate cancelled and excessive events
  Scenario: Migration scope preflight binds the SDK repository root
    Then migration scope preflight resolves files nested repositories and home attribution without granting history paths
  Scenario: Migration scope preflight rejects redirected sources and targets
    Then migration scopes reject ancestor repositories linked inputs and redirected native destinations
  Scenario: Migration source inventories detect changes and enforce limits
    Then migration source witnesses reject changed linked oversized and excessive files without returning their contents
  Scenario: Migration indirect sources retain private bounded ownership
    Then migration JSON readers and indirect references reject invalid escaped linked and changed sources
  Scenario: Migration effect verification requires persisted matching history
    Then migration effects reject missing history changed authority and unselected configuration namespaces
  Scenario: Migration receipts bind private adoption to the exact owned request
    Then migration authority receipts reject foreign hashes identities and malformed private values
  Scenario: Migration inputs leave space for authenticated framing
    Then migration byte limits preserve the longest owned envelope and reject the next byte by name
  Scenario: Migration preserves existing settings and private SQLite roots
    Then migration rejects overwritten existing settings and escaped or aliased plugin databases
  Scenario: Migration history lookup reads only the owned persisted record
    Then migration history readers preserve the database and reject malformed rows identifiers and aliases
  Scenario: Plugin migration follows selected provider source precedence
    Then plugin migration binds selected Claude and Cursor sources without following unused cache paths
  Scenario: Configured marketplaces stay inside owned migration sources
    Then configured plugin sources bind native caches and reject escaped or changed marketplace paths
  Scenario: Migration result projection retains metadata and withholds private text
    Then migration results withhold session derived text and native failures without accepting extra fields
